    <string name="help_body">"After connecting, battery information remains available with the viewfinder closed. Swipe anywhere inside the circular cover in any direction to open or close the viewfinder. Full-frame capture is available in Settings.\n\nCaptures belong to the active person. Ear labels can be edited in photo details. Settings includes profile management, personal cover images, default appearance, sounds and haptics.\n\nFor feedback, include the phone model, system version, steps and diagnostic log. Remove personal information first."</string>
    <string name="privacy_body">"The app receives device images over local Wi-Fi. It uses no accounts, advertising, analytics or cloud sync.\n\nProfile names, photos, ear labels, silent videos, known device Wi-Fi details and diagnostic logs are stored on your phone. Android requires permission to read the Wi-Fi list when finding nearby devices. The app does not scan the photo library. It reads only an image you explicitly choose, to crop and save a cover for the active person. Covers stay on your phone. The app does not access GPS, the microphone or Bluetooth.\n\nWhen you tap Share, Android passes your selected files to the app you choose. You can delete files from the gallery. Clearing app data or uninstalling removes its local data. Recipients control copies you have already shared.\n\nFor privacy questions or feedback, contact GitHub @foreverfine77."</string>
